## 2) Expanded group = tile with head

Structure (required):

```
.objaw-group
  ├── .objaw-q-bar     (head / question tab)
  └── .objaw-group-body
        └── .objaw-tags → .objaw-tag × N
```

### Head (`.objaw-q-bar`)

- Slightly black glass — **not** a solid dominating black plate.
- Background ≈ `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34)` + light blur (`blur(3px) saturate(160%)`).
- Thin dark border; overlaps body slightly (`margin-bottom: -12px`, higher z-index).
- Question text: thin gold `#C4A874` — quiet, not filled gold bars or white headlines.

### Body (`.objaw-group-body`)

- Radial vignette: **lighter center**, **darker edges** (e.g. center `rgba(0,0,0,~0.08)` → edge `~0.42`).
- Black / near-black frame (`border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.85)`).
- Padding leaves room under the overlapping head tab.

### Tags (`.objaw-tag`) — quiet

- Transparent fill, **black thin frame**, **white** label text.
- Gold pictorial **dot** before label: `::before` `7×7px` circle `#C4A874`.
- No marble fills, no silver glow flares, no heavy dispersion / bloom.
- Do not stretch tags into banners; keep chip proportions.

---

## Hard stops

- Do not replace this stack with opaque white cards, milky glass, or marble tag skins.
- Do not make the question head a solid black slab that kills the living-wall / depth read-through.
- When porting to another app: copy structure + glass tokens first; adapt only layout width / type scale if the host demands it — keep the head-and-body + quiet gold-dot tags.
